{
    "background_story": "Ayaan was a young Papuan tribesman from the remote island of New Guinea. Growing up in the dense rainforest, he learned the ancient traditions and customs of his people from his elders. Ayaan was particularly fascinated by the intricate wood carvings and storytelling that were an integral part of Papuan culture. As he honed his skills, he became known for his exquisite craftsmanship, creating beautiful masks and figurines that told stories of his ancestors. Ayaan's passion for preserving his cultural heritage led him to establish a community center where he taught the younger generation about their rich history and traditions. Through his work, Ayaan kept the Papuan spirit alive, ensuring that the stories and customs of his people would continue to thrive for generations to come.",
